From MOUSE mode, press ESC, W, A, S, or D to switch into KEYBOARD mode. 
To view the MAP of the area you are currently in, press the L key. 
Abusing a bug for personal gain will result in immediate banning without warning.
Abuse your account = Lose your account.
Type /s <playername> <message> to whisper to another player.
Type /p <message> to chat with all party members.
When not in chat mode, press M to reply to a whispered message.
Press R to switch to Auto-Run mode.
You may upgrade your class after reaching level 10.
SKILL POINTS increase after upgrading your class, you can learn various skills equal to the amount of Skill Points you have.
Taunting causes a monster to attack you.
Ex. ATTACK is the percentage of extra damage that is added to the final damage calculation.
Ex. DEFENSE is the percentage of damage that is decreased from the final damage calculation.
When STRENGTH (STR) increases, the amount of damage inflicted in close combat increases as well.
When DEXTERITY (DEX) increases, speed of movement, cool-down time, critical rate, and Ex. Defense increase as well.
When CONSTITUTION (CON) increases, the maximum HP and HP recovery amount increases.
When INTELLIGENCE (INT) increases, the Mage, Sorcerer, Enchanter, and Rune Officiator skills increase in power.
When INT increases, the amount of skill points available increases.
When WISDOM (WIS) increases, Acolytes, Priests, Clerics, and Life Officiator skills increase in power.
When WIS or INT is raised (whichever is higher), the maximum MP increases. 
MP recovery time increases according to the sum of INT and WIS.
Press C to rest and recover HP and MP faster.
Learning PASSIVE skills will improve your damage output for that skill.
PASSIVE skills cannot be placed into the quick slot bar.
K opens the SKILL window.
I opens INVENTORY.
U opens STATUS window.
Y opens SOCIETY window.
T opens the QUEST window.
Press F12 to take a screenshot.
Press F11 to open the Options window.
Skills in the QUICK SLOT bar may be selected by pressing keys 1~0.
You can place INSTANCE, CAST, and CHANT skills into the quick slot bar.
Items like bread, meat, and roast meat can be placed in the quick slot bar.
To use SPECIAL skills, select the appropriate skill from the quick slot (by pressing 1~0) and right-click.
To CAST a spell, select it and hold the right mouse button to charge your spell before letting go to complete the spell.
If you are attacked while casting a spell, the casting will be cancelled.
To use a CHANT, select it from the quick slot.
Use Z and X to switch between the first and second quick slots banks.
If you are human, press Q to change to the second weapon slot.
Hold down the middle mouse button to shift the camera angle with the mouse.
In MOUSE mode, you can turn the camera with the spacebar.
In KEYBOARD mode, press ESC to return to mouse mode.
Lower skills of other classes can only be learned after changing your class at level 10.
To redistribute STAT POINTS, you need a Stone of Oblivion, and you need to visit the Adventurer’s Trainer or Beginner’s Trainer.
Teleport Scrolls have a 15 second delay.
If you die while using a Teleport Scroll, the spell will be cancelled.
If you move while trying to use a Teleport Scroll, the spell will be cancelled.
A Teleport Scroll can be purchased at the general store of any town.
Teleport Scrolls can be placed into your quick slot bar.
You have 2.5 minutes to pick up an item / gold that is dropped from a monster.
You can start a whisper by clicking on a character's chat line in the chat window.